			],
			"Message": "refactor(Output): Standardize Tauri command names to PascalCase\n\nAlign the Tauri command invocations in the Output layer with the project-wide PascalCase naming convention. Update all process-related commands in `Source/Polyfill/Process/Polyfill.ts` (e.g., `process_get_exec_path` -> `ProcessGetExecPath`) and shared process health checks in `Source/Polyfill/Shared/Process/Proxy.ts` (e.g., `cocoon_extension_host_health` -> `CocoonExtensionHostHealth`).\n\nThis change ensures the TypeScript frontend correctly matches the Rust backend command definitions, which strictly adhere to the PascalCase standard across the CodeEditorLand architecture.",
			"SHA": "969a8ed1397074309224f98e40bc3213b0581ad5"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T15:33:09Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				751,
				3
			],
			"Message": "build(Output): Expand browserViewGroup IPC stubs and enable project references\n\nAdd the full set of expected communication channels for the `browserViewGroup` entry in the `StubChannels` record within the compiled Tauri Main Process Service artifact. Define `updateKeybindings`, `updateTheme`, `updateConfiguration`, `getBrowserViews`, `openDevTools`, and `closeDevTools` to align the Output layer with the UI requirements of the Sky component and Wind service layer.\n\nAdditionally, enable the `composite` flag in `tsconfig.json` to support project references. This ensures that type metadata is correctly generated for incremental builds and that the dependency graph between the Output artifacts and upstream Source TypeScript definitions remains consistent.\n\nNo runtime behavior is altered; these are structural updates to the build artifacts and TypeScript configuration to support the upcoming Tauri UI implementations.",
			"SHA": "bff9638d931568e0c5b79e08a8784897a6b0d674"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T10:13:19Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				751,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Output): Initialize browserViewGroup channels in TauriMainProcessService stub\n\nExpand the `browserViewGroup` entry in the `StubChannels` record within `Source/Service/Tauri/Main/Process/Service.ts` to define the full set of expected communication channels. This includes `updateKeybindings`, `updateTheme`, `updateConfiguration`, `getBrowserViews`, `openDevTools`, and `closeDevTools`.\n\nAligns the compiled Output artifact with the requirements of the upcoming Tauri UI implementations in Sky and Wind, ensuring that the IPC transform pipeline and runtime resolution logic have valid stub entries for all browser group operations before the native backend is fully wired.",
			"SHA": "6f571907334d9b133170adabb24cb92a838b19b3"
		}
